# APEX ADE Verification and Acceptance Testing

Complete acceptance testing plan and coding agent implementation brief

Version 1.1  |  Rust backend edition  |  23 October 2026

### Purpose

Verify that all 12 systems of the Agent Development Environment work through reproducible tests and saved evidence. A feature is complete only when appropriate automated tests demonstrate that its requirements are met. The existence of code, an endpoint or a UI control is not proof of functionality.

### Scope

This plan defines 96 system acceptance tests and 10 system-wide workflows. It includes testing tiers, deterministic fixtures, real boundary checks, infrastructure, pass criteria, evidence records, CI gates, implementation phases, reporting and the complete coding agent master prompt.

### Required decision

Use the initial repository audit to establish what exists, what is missing and what can be verified. Then implement the tests, execute them against the identified build and retain evidence before declaring a capability verified.

### Acceptance inventory

| Suite | Required cases | Readiness gate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| System acceptance | 96 | 8 of 8 per system |
| End-to-end acceptance | 10 | 10 of 10 workflows |
| Total | 106 | All required cases and evidence complete |

### Document use

Audience: the APEX owner, coding agent, maintainers and reviewers. This is a specification for verification, not an execution report. No passing result is asserted by this document. Record real results only after execution against a named revision and environment.

